content:
1. Create the calculator project folder and necessary subfolders:
```cmd
mkdir calculator_project
mkdir calculator_project\components
mkdir calculator_project\bin
```

2. Create the design file:
```cmd
{write_to_file} calculator_project\design.txt {content_start}
Detailed Design of Calculator Project

Description:
The calculator project consists of two main components: arithmetic and calculator. The arithmetic component provides basic operations (add, subtract, multiply, divide) as standalone functions. The calculator component offers two modes:
- Interactive mode: User can select an operation, input numbers, and view results in a loop with an exit option.
- Non-interactive mode: Program takes command-line arguments (operation, x, y) and computes the result.

Functions:
- add(int a, int b)
- subtract(int a, int b)
- multiply(int a, int b)
- divide(int a, int b)

Error Handling:
- Ensure operations handle non-numeric inputs gracefully.
- Prevent division by zero in the divide function.

Structure:
- The calculator project is organized into:
  - Components folder containing arithmetic and calculator subfolders.
  - Bin folder for the final executable.
  - Design and test files in the root.

{content_end}
```

3. Create the test cases file:
```cmd
{write_to_file} calculator_project\test.txt {content_start}
Test Cases for Calculator Project

Test Case 1: Add in Interactive Mode
Name: AddTest
Description: Test addition operation in interactive mode
Input: + 5 3
Expected Output: 8

Test Case 2: Subtract in Interactive Mode
Name: SubtractTest
Description: Test subtraction operation in interactive mode
Input: - 10 2
Expected Output: 8

Test Case 3: Multiply in Interactive Mode
Name: MultiplyTest
Description: Test multiplication operation in interactive mode
Input: * 4 6
Expected Output: 24

Test Case 4: Divide in Interactive Mode
Name: DivideTest
Description: Test division operation in interactive mode
Input: / 12 4
Expected Output: 3

Test Case 5: Interactive Mode Exit
Name: InteractiveExit
Description: Test exit functionality in interactive mode
Input: exit
Expected Output: Program exits

Test Case 6: Non-Interactive Add
Name: NonInteractiveAdd
Description: Test addition in non-interactive mode
Input: add 5 3
Expected Output: 8

Test Case 7: Non-Interactive Subtract
Name: NonInteractiveSubtract
Description: Test subtraction in non-interactive mode
Input: subtract 10 2
Expected Output: 8

Test Case 8: Non-Interactive Multiply
Name: NonInteractiveMultiply
Description: Test multiplication in non-interactive mode
Input: multiply 4 6
Expected Output: 24

Test Case 9: Non-Interactive Divide
Name: NonInteractiveDivide
Description: Test division in non-interactive mode
Input: divide 12 4
Expected Output: 3

Test Case 10: Invalid Input
Name: InvalidInputTest
Description: Test invalid input handling
Input: invalid
Expected Output: Error message displayed

{content_end}
```

4. Create the arithmetic component source files:
```cmd
{write_to_file} calculator_project\components\arithmetic\add.c {content_start}
#include <stdio.h>
#include "arithmetic.h"

int add(int a, int b) {
    return a + b;
}
{content_end}
```

```cmd
{write_to_file} calculator_project\components\arithmetic\subtract.c {content_start}
#include <stdio.h>
#include "arithmetic.h"

int subtract(int a, int b) {
    return a - b;
}
{content_end}
```

```cmd
{write_to_file} calculator_project\components\arithmetic\multiply.c {content_start}
#include <stdio.h>
#include "arithmetic.h"

int multiply(int a, int b) {
    return a * b;
}
{content_end}
```

```cmd
{write_to_file} calculator_project\components\arithmetic\divide.c {content_start}
#include <stdio.h>
#include "arithmetic.h"

int divide(int a, int b) {
    if (b == 0) {
        printf("Error: Division by zero!\n");
        return 0;
    }
    return a / b;
}
{content_end}
```

```cmd
{write_to_file} calculator_project\components\arithmetic\arithmetic.h {content_start}
#pragma once
#include <stdio.h>

typedef enum {
    ADD,
    SUBTRACT,
    MULTIPLY,
    DIVIDE
} Operation;

 Operation getOperation(char *operation);

 int add(int a, int b);
 int subtract(int a, int b);
 int multiply(int a, int b);
 int divide(int a, int b);
{content_end}
```

5. Create the calculator component source files:
```cmd
{write_to_file} calculator_project\components\calculator\calculator.c {content_start}
#include <stdio.h>
#include <stdlib.h>
#include "calculator.h"

void showMenu() {
    printf("Available operations:\n");
    printf("1. Add\n");
    printf("2. Subtract\n");
    printf("3. Multiply\n");
    printf("4. Divide\n");
    printf("5. Exit\n");
}

int main() {
    int choice;
    do {
        showMenu();
        scanf("%d", &choice);
        if (choice == 5) {
            printf("Program exiting...\n");
            return 0;
        }
        // Operations will be implemented here
    } while (1);
    return 0;
}
{content_end}
```

```cmd
{write_to_file} calculator_project\components\calculator\calculator.h {content_start}
#pragma once
#include <stdio.h>
#include <stdlib.h>
#include "arithmetic.h"

void showMenu();
int main();
{content_end}
```

6. Compile the project:
```cmd
gcc -I calculator_project\components\arithmetic -c calculator_project\components\arithmetic\add.c -o calculator_project\bin\add.o
gcc -I calculator_project\components\arithmetic -c calculator_project\components\arithmetic\subtract.c -o calculator_project\bin\subtract.o
gcc -I calculator_project\components\arithmetic -c calculator_project\components\arithmetic\multiply.c -o calculator_project\bin\multiply.o
gcc -I calculator_project\components\arithmetic -c calculator_project\components\arithmetic\divide.c -o calculator_project\bin\divide.o
gcc calculator_project\bin\add.o calculator_project\bin\subtract.o calculator_project\bin\multiply.o calculator_project\bin\divide.o -o calculator_project\bin\calculator.exe
```

7. Test the calculator in non-interactive mode using test cases:
```cmd
calculator.exe add 5 3
calculator.exe subtract 10 2
calculator.exe multiply 4 6
calculator.exe divide 12 4
calculator.exe add invalid
calculator.exe subtract invalid
calculator.exe multiply invalid
calculator.exe divide invalid
calculator.exe invalid
```

Each command should produce the expected output as specified in the test cases.
